A(('p', '13.3 Final Synthesis. A certain man is left half dead on the road from Jerusalem to Jericho. A priest and a Levite each see him and pass by on the other side, and a Samaritan sees him, has compassion, cares for him and pays for his keeping. Jesus asks which of the three was neighbour to him, the lawyer answers, “He that shewed mercy on him,” and Jesus says, “Go, and do thou likewise.”'))
