A(('call', 'Boundaries to Remember',
   'Jesus names “these three,” “him that fell among the thieves” and a command, and nothing more. No identity for the man, the thieves, the priest, the Levite, the Samaritan, the host, the oil, the wine, the inn or the two pence. No symbol carried in from another parable. Compassion, going to a man, binding wounds and paying are actions in a story, not steps of salvation. The Body of Christ is none of the figures in the story. The lessons are principles of conduct, not a transfer of Kingdom identity to the Body.'))
